# RAUC streams an update bundle over a network block device: every read of
# it is a download (25-system-update.md §5.5). When it connects, udev's
# blkid would probe it for file systems and RAID signatures, about a
# megabyte of buffered reads across the bundle, which the install then
# downloads again through dm-verity; nothing on the phone uses its links.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="nbd*", ENV{UDEV_DISABLE_PERSISTENT_STORAGE_RULES_FLAG}="1"
